          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Take samples of 10 with replacement and good mixing and estimate the proportion of red counters in the jar. Compare results.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Results vary. For each sample, the estimated red proportion is the number of red counters drawn divided by 10. Estimates from different samples may differ.",
      "worked": "After each draw, replace the counter and mix well before drawing again. Record the number of red counters in each sample of 10.\n\n$$\\text{Estimated red proportion}=\\frac{\\text{number of red counters in the sample}}{10}.$$\n\nSample result: 6 red counters gives an estimate of $\\frac{6}{10}=0.6=60\\%$. Compare the estimates from repeated samples; variation is expected even though the jar has not changed.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
